                <pb facs="0706" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.51A/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Price</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-28T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                                1921—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>78. Department’s 29, March 16, 5 p.m., complied with. I was authorized Saturday
                    through Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs to offer $12,000 salary to Fiscal
                    Agent Ruan to continue but latter refuses renewal of contract for less than
                    $15,000. I shall continue pressing matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
